      "message": "Possible command injection",
      "file": "bin/split_tests.rb",
      "line": 325,
      "note": "False positive. Two independent reasons: (1) system() is called in its ARRAY form - system(env, *argv) - which execs directly and never invokes a shell, so no command injection is possible regardless of the interpolated value; (2) the interpolated value goes through sanitize_db_identifier (bin/split_tests.rb:495), which strips everything outside [a-zA-Z0-9_] and double-quotes the result, so the SQL identifier is safe too. Brakeman's Execute check flags interpolation inside a system() argument without accounting for the non-shell array form. Unflagged by brakeman <= 8.0.5; first reported by 8.0.6 with no change to this file, which has been untouched since 2025-07-02."
    },
